# mr-vectors.golden — MR (MEMORY CHANNEL READ)
#
# ============================ SOURCE ============================
# Manual title as printed on cover:
#   "FTDX101MP / FTDX101D  CAT Operation Reference Manual"
#   (YAESU MUSEN CO., LTD.)
# Revision code as printed: 2308-L  (foot of final printed page, PDF 26)
# File consulted: docs/fixtures-private/manuals/ftdx101_cat_2308-L.pdf
#
# Position chart used:
#   Section heading "MR   MEMORY CHANNEL READ"
#   PRINTED page 16 (folio "16")  =  PDF page 17
#   (the MR section sits between "ML MONITOR LEVEL" above and
#    "MS METER SW" below — heading confirmed in the rendered image)
# Chart directions read:
#   vector 1 : the READ position chart (row labelled "Read")
#   vector 2 : the ANSWER position chart (row labelled "Answer")
#
# ---- DERIVATION METHOD -----------------------------------------
# Hand-derived from 400 dpi pdftoppm renders of PDF page 17, cropped and
# enlarged 160-170% with ImageMagick and read as images. No text
# extraction of any kind. Position-header rows sit ABOVE the token rows
# they number; this was respected throughout.
#
# ---- FIELD MAP: READ direction (1-based positions) -------------
#   pos 1   : "M"    (literal, chart)
#   pos 2   : "R"    (literal, chart)
#   pos 3-5 : P0     (3 positions) memory channel
#   pos 6   : ";"    (terminator, chart)
#   => Read frame length 6 bytes including the ";".
#   Positions 7-10 of the Read row are printed blank.
#
# ---- FIELD MAP: ANSWER direction (1-based positions) -----------
#   pos  1     : "M"                 (literal, chart)
#   pos  2     : "R"                 (literal, chart)
#   pos  3- 5  : P1  (3 positions)   memory channel
#   pos  6-14  : P2  (9 positions)   VFO-A Frequency (Hz)
#   pos 15-19  : P3  (5 positions)   clarifier direction (1) + offset (4)
#   pos 20     : P4  (1 position)    RX CLAR
#   pos 21     : P5  (1 position)    TX CLAR
#   pos 22     : P6  (1 position)    MODE
#   pos 23     : P7  (1 position)    VFO / Memory
#   pos 24     : P8  (1 position)    CTCSS
#   pos 25-26  : P9  (2 positions)   (Fixed)
#   pos 27     : P10 (1 position)    repeater shift
#   pos 28     : ";"                 (terminator, chart)
#   => Answer frame length 28 bytes including the ";".
#   The Answer grid's third header row runs 21..30 with tokens
#   P5 P6 P7 P8 P9 P9 P10 ";" and positions 29-30 blank.
#
# ---- PARAMETER LEGEND as printed beside the MR charts ----------
#   P0   001-099 (Memory Channel), P1L -P9U (PMS), 5xx (5MHz BAND),
#        EMG (EMERGENCY CH)
#   P2   VFO-A Frequency (Hz)
#   P3   Clarifier Direction +: Plus Shift, --: Minus Shift
#        Clarifier Offset: 0000 - 9990 (Hz)
#   P4   0: RX CLAR "OFF"    1: RX CLAR "ON"
#   P5   0: TX CLAR "OFF"    1: TX CLAR "ON"
#   P6   MODE 1: LSB  2: USB  3: CW-U  4: FM  5: AM  6: RTTY-L  7: CW-L
#             8: DATA-L  9: RTTY-U  A: DATA-FM  B: FM-N  C: DATA-U
#             D: AM-N  E: PSK  F: DATA-FM-N
#   P7   0: VFO  1: Memory
#   P8   0: CTCSS "OFF"   1: CTCSS ENC/DEC   2: CTCSS ENC
#   P9   00: (Fixed)
#   P10  0: Simplex   1: Plus Shift   2: Minus Shift
#   (There is NO "P1" line in the MR legend — see anomaly N1 below.)
#
# ---- BYTE-BY-BYTE PROVENANCE -----------------------------------
# VECTOR 1  read_request_ch007   "MR007;"
#   pos 1-2  "MR"  MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid positions 1, 2.
#   pos 3-5  "007" MANUAL-DOCUMENTED as a field — Read grid positions
#            3-5 are P0; value 007 is documented-legal by legend line
#            "P0 001-099 (Memory Channel)". Choice of 007: assumption A4.
#   pos 6    ";"   MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Read grid terminator cell.
#
# VECTOR 2  answer_ch007_usb_14m250
#            "MR007014250000+000000210000;"
#   pos 1-2   "MR"        MANUAL-DOCUMENTED (Answer grid).
#   pos 3-5   "007"       field MANUAL-DOCUMENTED (P1, 3 wide);
#                         VALUE vocabulary inherited — see anomaly N1.
#   pos 6-14  "014250000" field MANUAL-DOCUMENTED (P2, 9 wide, "Hz");
#                         leading-zero padding is assumption A2.
#   pos 15    "+"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P3 "+: Plus Shift".
#   pos 16-19 "0000"      MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend "Clarifier Offset:
#                         0000 - 9990 (Hz)", 0000 being the lower bound.
#                         Pairing "+" with zero is assumption A3.
#   pos 20    "0"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P4 0: RX CLAR "OFF".
#   pos 21    "0"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P5 0: TX CLAR "OFF".
#   pos 22    "2"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P6 2: USB.
#   pos 23    "1"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P7 1: Memory
#                         (READ/ANSWER direction vocabulary; the Set-only
#                         "(Fixed)" wording of the sibling MT command does
#                         not apply here).
#   pos 24    "0"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P8 0: CTCSS "OFF".
#   pos 25-26 "00"        MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P9 "00: (Fixed)".
#   pos 27    "0"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — legend P10 0: Simplex.
#   pos 28    ";"         MANUAL-DOCUMENTED — Answer grid terminator cell.
#
# INHERITED ASSUMPTIONS
#   A2  Leading-zero padding of P2 to fill all 9 positions. Inferred from
#       the fixed field width; not printed.
#       LIFTED BY: any real-radio MR Answer for an HF channel.
#   A3  "+" chosen as the direction accompanying a zero clarifier offset;
#       the manual does not say which sign a zero offset carries.
#       LIFTED BY: a captured MR Answer for a channel with clarifier off /
#       zero offset.
#   A4  Choice of channel 007, frequency 14.250000 MHz and mode USB.
#       Free choices inside documented ranges; not claims about the radio.
#       LIFTED BY: not applicable.
#   A7  That the Answer's P1 uses the same channel-number vocabulary as
#       the Read's P0. The MR legend prints only a P0 line (anomaly N1);
#       the identity of P1's vocabulary is inherited from the sibling MT
#       command, whose legend line is labelled "P0/1".
#       LIFTED BY: a captured MR Answer for a known channel — positions
#       3-5 of the reply confirm the vocabulary directly.
#   A8  That a real Answer echoes the same channel number that was
#       requested. Not stated by the manual.
#       LIFTED BY: an MR Read/Answer round trip on a real radio.
#
# ---- ANOMALY OBSERVED (recorded, not resolved) -----------------
#   N1  The MR parameter legend has no "P1" line. Its first line is
#       labelled "P0" and covers 001-099 / PMS / 5xx / EMG, yet the
#       Answer grid's positions 3-5 are labelled P1. The neighbouring MT
#       command's equivalent line is labelled "P0/1", which suggests the
#       MR line should read "P0/1" too. Recorded, not corrected.
#   N2  The legend's minus-shift direction is printed as two hyphen
#       glyphs, "--: Minus Shift", in every one of MR / MT / MW. Since P3
#       is only 5 positions wide and the offset alone is documented as 4
#       digits, the direction can occupy just one position; the printed
#       "--" is therefore taken to be a typographic rendering, not two
#       bytes. No vector in this file uses a minus direction, so no byte
#       here depends on the reading. Recorded, not resolved.
#
# ---- HARDWARE STATUS -------------------------------------------
#   UNVERIFIED. Neither frame has been sent to, or captured from, a real
#   FTDX101MP or FTDX101D.
#
# Derivation date: 06/08/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document or web
# resource was consulted — only the single PDF named above.
#
read_request_ch007	MR007;
answer_ch007_usb_14m250	MR007014250000+000000210000;
